{{!-- What the post is filed under, closing the article.

Every tag, not just the primary one, because this is the row a reader uses to find the rest of
the subject — and each chip is a link to that tag's own archive, which is the Surface the
design's chips only imply.

`visibility="public"` is the whole reason this is {{#foreach}} and not a hand-rolled loop over
`tags`: a Ghost publication uses internal tags (`#featured`, `#newsletter-only`) as private
editorial routing, and printing them on the page leaks the newsroom's own filing system to
every reader.

The guard is `primary_tag` for the same reason — it IS the post's first public tag, so it is
exactly the condition "there is at least one chip to draw". `{{#if tags}}` is satisfied by a post
filed only under internal tags, and would render the rule and the label with nothing after
them. --}}
{{#if primary_tag}}
	<hr class="border-border mt-14 border-0 border-t">

	<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5">
		<span class="text-muted mr-1.5 font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Filed under"}}</span>

		{{#foreach tags visibility="public"}}
			<a
				href="{{url}}"
				class="font-meta tracking-meta border-border bg-surface text-text rounded-pill border px-3.5 py-[7px] text-[12.5px] uppercase no-underline">{{name}}</a>
		{{/foreach}}
	</div>
{{/if}}
